{"title":"Career roadmap · Forensics Assistant","role":"Forensics Assistant","summary":"A Forensics Assistant supports the collection, preservation, examination and documentation of digital evidence during cybersecurity incidents, investigations and legal proceedings. In a BCA Cyber Security pathway, the strongest route is digital forensics, with foundations in networking, operating systems, incident response and evidence handling.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BCA (Bachelor of Computer Applications)","Course":"BCA – Cyber Security / Ethical Hacking","Timeline assumption":"3-year BCA beginning in 2026 → graduation around 2029. For a 4-year honours structure, graduation would typically be around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Direct"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BCA Cybersecurity","Digital Forensics + Networking + Linux/Windows","Forensics Internship","Forensics Assistant / Junior Digital Forensics Analyst","Digital Forensics Analyst","Senior Investigator / Incident Response Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"For government investigative roles, recruitment requirements vary by organisation and post. A private-sector digital-forensics role can often be entered through cybersecurity skills, internships and demonstrable lab experience."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What to focus on"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2029/30"},{"text":"Build cybersecurity, OS, networking, evidence-handling and digital-forensics fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2029–2034"},{"text":"Develop professional experience in forensic examination, incident response and security investigations."}],[{"text":"2034–2040"},{"text":"Specialise in DFIR, malware forensics, mobile/cloud forensics or cybercrime investigations."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Forensics Lead, Incident Response Lead, Digital Forensics Manager, Consultant or specialised investigator."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Computing fundamentals"},{"text":"Programming + computer architecture"},{"text":"Small Python/C programs"},{"text":"Technical foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Networking + Linux"},{"text":"TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP, Linux"},{"text":"Home lab"},{"text":"Infrastructure knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Authentication, vulnerabilities, attacks"},{"text":"Secure-system lab"},{"text":"Security foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Digital forensics"},{"text":"Disk, filesystem and evidence concepts"},{"text":"Forensic case reports"},{"text":"Forensics readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Incident response"},{"text":"Logs, timelines, IOC analysis"},{"text":"Incident investigation"},{"text":"DFIR capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Internship + advanced labs"},{"text":"Windows, memory, network and mobile forensics"},{"text":"Forensic portfolio"},{"text":"Job readiness"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Cloud/mobile/malware forensics"},{"text":"Advanced case study"},{"text":"Specialisation"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Professional readiness"},{"text":"Reporting, interviews, certification"},{"text":"Capstone + internship"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects to prioritise"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer Networks"},{"text":"Operating Systems"},{"text":"Computer Architecture"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Data Structures"},{"text":"Database Management"},{"text":"Cybersecurity Fundamentals"},{"text":"Network Security"},{"text":"Ethical Hacking"},{"text":"Digital Forensics"},{"text":"Cybercrime Investigation"},{"text":"Incident Response"},{"text":"Cryptography"},{"text":"Malware Analysis"},{"text":"Information Security"},{"text":"Cyber Law"},{"text":"Cloud Security"},{"text":"Mobile Security"},{"text":"Security Operations"},{"text":"Research Methodology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Operating systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Windows internals"},{"text":"Filesystems"},{"text":"Permissions"},{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Registry"},{"text":"Event logs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Networking"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TCP/IP"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"},{"text":"HTTP/HTTPS"},{"text":"VPNs"},{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"Packet analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Disk imaging"},{"text":"File-system analysis"},{"text":"Deleted-file recovery"},{"text":"Timeline analysis"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Hashing"},{"text":"Evidence preservation"},{"text":"Chain of custody"},{"text":"Forensic reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Autopsy"},{"text":"The Sleuth Kit"},{"text":"FTK Imager"},{"text":"Volatility"},{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"Zeek"},{"text":"KAPE"},{"text":"Eric Zimmerman tools"},{"text":"YARA"},{"text":"Ghidra"},{"text":"Burp Suite"},{"text":"Nmap"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use only owned, authorised or deliberately vulnerable environments when practising security techniques."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio target"},{"type":"p","text":"Build 5–7 documented forensic investigations using legally safe datasets or lab environments:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Windows event-log investigation"},{"text":"Disk-image investigation"},{"text":"Deleted-file recovery case"},{"text":"Network packet investigation"},{"text":"Memory-forensics case"},{"text":"Phishing/email-header investigation"},{"text":"Incident-response timeline"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Each case should contain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case objective"},{"text":"Evidence source"},{"text":"Hash values"},{"text":"Acquisition method"},{"text":"Tools used"},{"text":"Investigation timeline"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Indicators of compromise"},{"text":"Evidence limitations"},{"text":"Final report"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Disk Forensics"},{"text":"Filesystems, imaging, recovery"},{"text":"Forensic labs"},{"text":"Senior Forensic Analyst"}],[{"text":"Windows Forensics"},{"text":"Registry, Event Logs, artifacts"},{"text":"DFIR labs"},{"text":"Windows Forensics Specialist"}],[{"text":"Memory Forensics"},{"text":"RAM analysis, Volatility"},{"text":"Incident-response labs"},{"text":"Memory Forensics Specialist"}],[{"text":"Network Forensics"},{"text":"Wireshark, Zeek, PCAP"},{"text":"SOC/DFIR teams"},{"text":"Network Forensics Analyst"}],[{"text":"Mobile Forensics"},{"text":"Android/iOS artifacts"},{"text":"Mobile forensic labs"},{"text":"Mobile Forensics Specialist"}],[{"text":"Cloud Forensics"},{"text":"Cloud logs, IAM, storage"},{"text":"Cloud security teams"},{"text":"Cloud Forensics Specialist"}],[{"text":"Malware Forensics"},{"text":"Static/dynamic analysis"},{"text":"Malware labs"},{"text":"Malware Analyst"}],[{"text":"Incident Response"},{"text":"SIEM, EDR, IOC analysis"},{"text":"SOC/CSIRT teams"},{"text":"DFIR Lead"}],[{"text":"Cybercrime Investigation"},{"text":"Evidence + investigation"},{"text":"Law-enforcement ecosystem"},{"text":"Cybercrime Investigator"}],[{"text":"eDiscovery"},{"text":"Digital evidence + legal workflows"},{"text":"Legal-tech teams"},{"text":"eDiscovery Specialist"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital evidence will increasingly come from cloud platforms, mobile devices, SaaS applications, IoT systems, encrypted storage and AI-enabled systems. Forensics professionals will therefore need to understand cloud logging, identity systems, endpoint telemetry, threat intelligence, automation and